-- the theorem the field states informally and then cannot enforce: an observation of an atom that
-- is invariant under the automorphisms is constant on orbits. This is what makes "chemically
-- equivalent positions" a property of the molecule rather than of a drawing — the NMR count, the
-- equivalent hydrogens of a methyl group, the symmetry-related atoms of a crystallographic site.
-- No finiteness, no set-hood and no truncation is used: the witness carries the whole argument.
orbit-invariant : (M : Mol) → (B : Type 0) → (f : mol-atoms M → B)
                → ((a : Auto M) → (x : mol-atoms M) → f (auto-fun M a x) ≡ f x)
                → (x : mol-atoms M) → (y : mol-atoms M) → Orbit M x y → f x ≡ f y
orbit-invariant M B f h x y o = concat (sym (h (fst o) x)) (cong f (snd o))
